  var result = eval(script);
  print(result);
  return result;
}

var result = runScript("myFunction();");
```

It's worth noting that Bitburner's scripting environment is designed to be a sandboxed environment, and some functions may not be available or may behave differently than in a standard Node.js environment. Be sure to test your scripts thoroughly to ensure they work as expected.

